ULTRALYTICS TRACKER DEFAULTS
============================

`mosaic track ultralytics` selects one of six tracker backends Ultralytics
ships. Their default settings are transcribed -- the setting names and
their values, in mosaic's own structure -- into
src/mosaic/tracking/ultralytics_track/tracker_defaults.py from
ultralytics/cfg/trackers/{botsort,bytetrack,ocsort,deepocsort,fasttrack,
tracktrack}.yaml as of Ultralytics 8.4.63. The YAML files themselves are
not copied and no AGPL-licensed source is vendored into src/.

The backends implement published methods. Results produced with one should
cite it:

  ByteTrack. Zhang, Y. et al. (2021). ByteTrack: Multi-Object Tracking by
  Associating Every Detection Box. arXiv:2110.06864.

  BoT-SORT. Aharon, N., Orfaig, R., Bobrovsky, B.-Z. (2022). BoT-SORT:
  Robust Associations Multi-Pedestrian Tracking. arXiv:2206.14651.

  OC-SORT. Cao, J. et al. (2022). Observation-Centric SORT: Rethinking
  SORT for Robust Multi-Object Tracking. arXiv:2203.14360.

  Deep OC-SORT. Maggiolino, G. et al. (2023). Deep OC-SORT:
  Multi-Pedestrian Tracking by Adaptive Re-Identification.
  arXiv:2302.11813.

  FastTracker. Hashempoor, H., Hwang, Y. D. (2025). FastTracker:
  Real-Time and Accurate Visual Tracking. arXiv:2508.14370.

  TrackTrack. Shim et al. (2025). Focusing on Tracks for Online
  Multi-Object Tracking. CVPR 2025.


