FETCHED MODEL WEIGHTS
=====================

Mosaic distributes no weights. The terms are the ones the hub entry states
at the moment of download.

FERAL backbones, built at first use.

  V-JEPA 2 and V-JEPA 2.1, from facebookresearch/vjepa2 and the
  facebook/vjepa2-* hub entries. The repository states that "The majority
  of V-JEPA 2 is licensed under MIT, however portions of the project are
  available under separate license terms"; three files are Apache-2.0.
  Each facebook/vjepa2-* card mosaic can reach declares MIT. The default,
  facebook/vjepa2-vitl-fpc32-256-diving48, declares MIT.

  VideoPrism, from the sposiboh/videoprism-*-pt hub entries. These are
  third-party PyTorch ports, not Google DeepMind's own release, and each
  port's card declares Apache-2.0. Upstream google-deepmind/videoprism
  licenses its code under Apache-2.0 and states that "All other materials
  are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  License (CC-BY)", which covers the weights. The two declarations have
  not been reconciled by either party. A user who needs certainty should
  obtain the weights from DeepMind directly and observe CC-BY-4.0
  attribution.

Identity backbones, loaded through timm by global-identity-embedding.
The default, timm/swin_large_patch4_window12_384.ms_in22k_ft_in1k, is MIT.

  MegaDescriptor. https://huggingface.co/BVRA/MegaDescriptor-L-384

      Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
      (CC-BY-NC-4.0). Non-commercial use only.

  BVRA/MegaDescriptor-L-384 and BVRA/MegaDescriptor-T-224 both declare
  CC-BY-NC-4.0. The restriction is on the trained parameters, not on
  mosaic's code and not on the architecture. Mosaic never selects
  MegaDescriptor; naming it is the user's act.

  DINOv2. Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
  Apache-2.0. https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov2
  Loaded through torch.hub by the DINOv2 identity backbone.


